# Shadow-reviewer shared suggestions file (INFRA-358) — advisory mid-build
# steering channel, written inside a story worktree by the concurrent
# shadow-reviewer and polled by the builder. Never committed, never part of
# any story's diff, never treated by the reviewer as story artifact.
.pairmode-suggestions.md

# Ephemeral notes and screenshots (not record-keeping)
flex_eph/

# Vendored dependency payload (CER-090 / INFRA-261) — deliberate override of the
# global dist/ and build/ patterns above. Those target *our* build output; inside a
# vendored node_modules they also exclude shipped package payload (compiled JS and
# .d.ts), which leaves every fresh git worktree unable to run `pnpm --filter
# @flex-obs/ui build`. Do not remove these lines to "clean up" the file.
!**/node_modules/**/dist/
!**/node_modules/**/build/
# ...except node-gyp compile intermediates (~15 MB of .o files): rebuildable, never
# loaded at runtime. The compiled addon beside them (better_sqlite3.node) IS tracked.
**/node_modules/**/build/Release/obj/
**/node_modules/**/build/Release/obj.target/
# ...and better-sqlite3's second gyp target (CER-094 / INFRA-307): a test fixture
# for that package's own loadExtension test suite, never loaded by this project
# (better-sqlite3/lib/database.js:48 requires only better_sqlite3.node). Deleted
# from the tracked payload; `pnpm rebuild better-sqlite3` regenerates it on disk,
# so it must stay ignored rather than resurface as an offending untracked file.
**/node_modules/**/build/Release/test_extension.node

# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo (CER-070 addendum / INFRA-302) — a pure incremental
# *typecheck* cache (ui/tsconfig.json sets "noEmit": true), rewritten by
# `tsc -b` on every UI-build-gate run, including failing ones, which dirties a
# story worktree and makes merge-story-worktree's rebase refuse. Its paired
# output (ui/dist) is already ignored; tracking one half of an incremental
# pair is how a `tsc -b` gets talked out of doing any work. Regenerated on
# demand and has no reader.
/skills/observability/ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# vitest cache (INFRA-312) — `skills/observability/api/vitest.config.ts` pins
# `cacheDir` to this path (rather than vitest's default `node_modules/.vite`)
# specifically so it can be ignored precisely: `pnpm test` rewrites a
# results.json under a content-hash subdirectory on every run, including
# failing ones, which otherwise leaves an untracked file inside the tracked
# vendored `node_modules` payload (CER-090 / INFRA-261) and dirties a story
# worktree the same way tsconfig.tsbuildinfo above did. Pure run-cache,
# regenerated on demand, no reader.
/skills/observability/api/node_modules/.vitest-cache/
